                                                                  9131 1451
 FILE ASSEMBLY, VERIFICATION AND VALIDATION                       9131 1451
 A. Trkov, IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                  9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 The ENDF-formatted data from EMPIRE calculation were merged      9131 1451
 consistently with the resonance data (see description below).    9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 Average number of delayed neutrons and delayed neutron spectra   9131 1451
 were taken from JENDL-3.3 and extrapolated flat to 60 MeV.       9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 The assembled file was checked according to the IAEA             9131 1451
 verification procedure [1]. None of the checking codes reported  9131 1451
 any significant warnings. Comparison with experimental data      9131 1451
 from EXFOR confirmed that the data are representative of the     9131 1451
 database on which the evaluation is based. The ACE file for      9131 1451
 Monte Carlo transport calculations was produced as a result of   9131 1451
 the checking process, including standard plots. No specific      9131 1451
 benchmarks sensitive to Pa-231 data were identified, therefore   9131 1451
 further validation could not be performed. Plots and other       9131 1451
 details are available on the above-defined web page of the CRP.  9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 [1] A. Trkov: Guidelines for Nuclear Data Verification and       9131 1451
     Validation, International Atomic Energy Agency, Vienna,      9131 1451
     Austria, INDC(SEC)-0107, August 2005.                        9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
