 FAST ENERGY REGION                                               9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 Authors:                                                         9131 1451
 Roberto Capote (IAEA/NAPC, Nuclear Data Section)                 9131 1451
 Mihaela Sin (University of Bucharest, Romania)                   9131 1451
 Andrej Trkov (IAEA/NAPC, Nuclear Data Section)                   9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 EVALUATION PROCEDURE                                             9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                9131 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               9131 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              9131 1451
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-2.19b33 by                    9131 1451
 M. Herman et al [He01, He02]. This code integrates               9131 1451
 into a single system a number of important modules               9131 1451
 and features, relevant for this evaluation:                      9131 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 9131 1451
   coupled-channels (ECIS03 by J. Raynal)                         9131 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    9131 1451
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              9131 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      9131 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 9131 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                9131 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   9131 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                9131 1451
   discrete transitions                                           9131 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL-2 library [Ri03]              9131 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                9131 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               9131 1451
   and gamma strength functions  based on the RIPL-2              9131 1451
   library [Ri03]                                                 9131 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              9131 1451
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           9131 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    9131 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 9131 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                9131 1451
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      9131 1451
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        9131 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 9131 1451
 current evaluation:                                              9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-2 level                 9131 1451
 file, based on the 1998 version of ENSDF.                        9131 1451
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  9131 1451
 Exclusive spectra available up to emission loop #  3             9131 1451
 Coupled Channels (ECIS) used for direct inelastic scattering     9131 1451
 Width fluctuations calculated within HRTW  up to 0.90 MeV        9131 1451
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS                      9131 1451
 Cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model            9131 1451
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)           9131 1451
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS set to  1.7 (Recommended ~ 1.59131 1451
 Max hole number in PCROSS set to 0.20*sqrt(g*U)                  9131 1451
    being U the CN excitation energy                              9131 1451
 Emission width of ejectile 0 from 232Pa multiplied by   1.300    9131 1451
 For all nuclei: advanced treatment of fission                    9131 1451
 Prompt fission neutron spectra and nu-bar calculation include    9131 1451
 contributions from Pa and Th chains (see description of the      9131 1451
 method in Maslov V.M. et al, Eur.Phys.J.A18(2003)93).            9131 1451
 Calculations were carried out with a new EMPIRE PFNS module      9131 1451
 developed by R. Capote and M. Sin. Nu-bar evaluation at thermal  9131 1451
 energy is based on calculations carried out by A. Tudora,        9131 1451
 G. Vladuca and F.-J.Hambsch. Above the first fission chance both 9131 1451
 post-fission and pre-fission neutrons were considered.           9131 1451
 Prefission neutrons angular distribution assumed anisotropic     9131 1451
 following (n,xn) distribution.                                   9131 1451
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  9131 1451
 E1 strength function set to MLO1                                 9131 1451
 GDR parameters from RIPL-2/Exp.data+Plujko systematics           9131 1451
