  RESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETER                                    9131 1451
  S.F. Mughabghab, L. Leal                                        9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
  The resolved MLBW resonance parameters were evaluated by S.F    9131 1451
  Mughabghab. A bound level is postulated to fit the thermal      9131 1451
  constants [1]. In addition, to fit a bound coherent scattering  9131 1451
  amplitude of 9.3 fm, a potential scattering  radiu of 10.4 fm   9131 1451
  was required, which is  larger than the systematics in this     9131 1451
  mass region. With these parameters the following thermal        9131 1451
  constants are obtained:                                         9131 1451
    capture=200.7 b                                               9131 1451
    scattering= 11.2 b                                            9131 1451
    fission   = 0.020 b                                           9131 1451
    capture resonance integral=536b including contribution        9131 1451
                                    from the unresolved region.   9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
  Fission widths above 60 eV that were zero were assigned a       9131 1451
  width of 5E-6 eV (recommendation by L. Leal).                   9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
  Some additional reformulation of the parameters was done by     9131 1451
  L. Leal. The resonance parameters were converted into           9131 1451
  Reich-Moore formalism an covariances were generated from the    9131 1451
  quoted uncertainties of the resonance parameters.               9131 1451
                                                                  9131 1451
 [1] S.F. Mughabghab, Atlas of Neutron Resonances, Elsevier,2006. 9131 1451
